      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-25_WidnesExaminer_art0030" n="art0030">
        <head>SILVER ORE IN NOVA scon A.</head>
        <p>SILVER ORE IN NOVA scon A.</p>
        <p>An important deposit oi lead silver one recently dis- covered In Cape Breton, Nova Scotia, in attracting attention. The One body °more as a Motions body amesging 30 feet in width along the line of contact between porphyry and highly charged limestone. Trial pits and cross-cots have promo the ore for a length exceeding 1003 feet, and annoy values run from 56 doll. to 260d015. for the ton. The engine., who reported on the find my. that the property appeals to him ea one of the most important ore bodim ever found east of the Rocky Mountains. A recent census gives the population of Calgary at 55,330, an increase of 9,000 in the past year. Calgary's growth in this year. directory show, that there is in that city a greater proportion of English-speaking people than in almoet any other city in the wt.</p>
        <p>A Illy th pilot who was drowned on Satorday weighed ant., aod it was stated at the Milne/it that two men who went to hia rescue in a cutter had to lash him to the stern with his head above water and tow the body aahore.</p>
