      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-25_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>MASTER BUILDERS ASSOCIATION.</head>
        <p>MASTER BUILDERS ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>kennel Dinner.</p>
        <p>The annual dinner of the Warrington Master Builders' Association was held at the Patten Arms on Thursday evening. There was an excellent attend- ance of about (11, and amongst those present were the Minor Coumillor lie Jtisepn!, Mr. 11. Chin ) presi- dent of the association(, Mr. T. I. mgdin ilmrough !surveyor), Mr. J. Gray water engineer), Mr. Frank Woods (president of the Lancashire, Cheshire, and North Walee Budding Trade Employers' Federation , and Messrs. T. (7,urran, W. Walter, H. Mallard, C. E. Bunch, R. H. Daiutith, J. L Davenport, C. H. Wells, C. W. Davenport, J. Dolan, H. Fairclongb, S. Warburton, T. Cooper, W. Winataoley, 3. B. Johnson, H. Rogers, H. Bibby, and J. H. Smethurst. After the loyal toasts bad been honoured, Mr. Frank Woods proposed the toast of "The Master Builders. Association, which was responded to by the President(Mr. Harry Collin). " 'he town and trade of Warrington" was proposed by Mr. 3. H. Smethurst, and responded to by his Worship the Mayor. The toasts of "Oar Guest," was entrusted to Mr. Dolan, and Messrs. T. Curran, H. Ballard, and W. Walter, whilst " The Corporation officials " was pro- kosed by Mr. H. Fairclaugh, and replied to by Messrs Longdin and James Gray. uriug the evening a capital programme of music was supplied by the Warrington Male Voice Quartette, cum' ting of Mossrs. Gough, Willett, Boscow and Whitt e. Mr. H. Ballard ako contributed some very amusi g Lancashire sketches in an intensely humorous manne</p>
        <p>, - CONGO HORRORS. P ESENTATION TO MR. F. D. 1110F;EL. ~t In co ide_ration of the excelleut and voluntary work which h been accomplished by Mr. F. D. Morel on behalf the natives of the Congo basin, • national testiruon al is to be presented to rum. Is is claimed to be poetic 'arty fitting that the Free Cherokee !Mould take surge a are in the testimonial, and several prominent members of the National Free Church Council, headed by Dr. J watt, have issoed a letter to Free Churchmen, requesti g them to help in making the Free Church contrib ion as large as possible. HAR V.—Your Mood is quite correct. The 'Orchid' ra ors are made for light, medium, or heavy shav- ing and re unequelled.—Oncrf ID MANUFACTURING CO. 146, Br st., Birmingham. But all Ironmongers end Cutlers supply them. No, there is nothing better made ....11.</p>
