        <p>THE RISE OF THE ROTHSCHTLIY The death of Baron Albert von Rothschild the Vienna banking-house, reminds us the century and a half have gone since Meyer Rothechild, founder of the family fortunes, n back ou the unsavoury Judengrisse, in a I slum, in which he had been cradled, and tn Hanover in quest of fortune. Whoa, fifty ye he lay dying—a millionaire end the financial of Europe—he summoned his five sons to hi and, with much good counsel, urged on them I should conduct the great business he had be. partnership,trusting each other and working in for the expansion of the family fortune.. 0 sons, Anselm remained at Frankfort, Solon his headquarters at Vienna, Nathan in Regime at Naples, and James at Paris. In 1818 the Francis of Auatria ennobled all the five bn recognition of their great financial service yearn later each of them was a Baron. Thai grew by leaps and hounds ; they were le Europe and the arbiters of national destinies.</p>
